:null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":null,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":0.38820729744274973,"_gp_pool_share":true,"_score_pool_share":100.0,"_gate_rev_durability":0.12160661576100784,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":85.8,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.00874915051730335,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":20.8,"_gate_share_shrink":0.04187575847444225,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.012176090464911327,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":79.7,"_gate_insider_own":0.14661,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":97.7,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"HCI Group, Inc., together with its subsidiaries, engages in the property and casualty insurance business in the United States. The company operates through Insurance Operations, Exzeo, Reciprocal Exchange Operations, and Real Estate segments. It provides homeowners' property and casualty insurance products; claim adjusting and processing services; turnkey insurance technology and operations solutions to property and casualty insurance carriers and its agents through the Exzeo platform; and SAMSTM, a web-based system designed to automate and streamline the process of managing insurance policies. The company also offers Harmony, a policy administration platform; ClaimColony, an end-to-end claims management platform; AtlasViewer, a mapping and data visualization platform. In addition, it is involved in reciprocal exchange operations; and developing and operating commercial properties for investment purposes. The company was formerly known as Homeowners Choice, Inc. and changed its name to HCI Group, Inc. in May 2013. HCI Group, Inc. was incorporated in 2006 and is headquartered in Tampa, Florida.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Pareshbhai Suryakant Patel | Founder, Chairman, President & CEO | Age 62 | Compensation: $8.2M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 594 people. Revenue per employee of $1.5M ranks in the top quartile among Financial Services peers, with revenue growing 17%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $742K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $18K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 5\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (10/10).","financial_summary":["HCI Group, Inc. is a mid-cap financial services business with a $2.4B market cap on $901M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +22% over the past three years and +12% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder. Operating margins are expanding by +2.2pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at 18% against a 9% cost of capital, a 9-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","The business throws off $441M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 49 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.49\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage of 48\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield is only 0.9%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 15% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and within its sector the business captures 1.9\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 5.7% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 20% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Trading at a 70% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Valued at a 66% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","15 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Growing faster than most Financial Services peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool"],"news_